      "writtenOn": "2022-07-13T23:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "oh, now I understand. I was simply trying to reproduce your EOF issue and couldn\u0027t.\n\nold Jython starts but prints an error.\n\nJython 2.5.2 has one small advantage - it does not need \"Lib\" directory to be linked in (even the doc says it is optional) and therefore easier to set up. For Jython 2.7 we should probably provide a better instructions (setting python.home, maybe?)\n\nBut since global variables get printed anyway, what about we get rid of printing this stuff in that file at all?",
      "parentUuid": "3cf99bd3_21a27433",
      "revId": "a793805549415dbbdaf125296a8e4b884cb2def2",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
