      "writtenOn": "2022-07-14T10:41:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for the confusion, the EOF error is issue 16068 and I think it is a version mismatch for antlr. It only happens with the Debian package and is an entirely different issue indeed.\n\n\u003e But since global variables get printed anyway, what about we get rid of printing this stuff in that file at all? \n\nThen I guess we can drop the Startup.py entirely?",
      "parentUuid": "e2aac100_bf9a68ad",
      "revId": "a793805549415dbbdaf125296a8e4b884cb2def2",
